# Proxy image vulnerability exceptions.
#
# Keep this file empty unless a HIGH/CRITICAL finding has no available patched
# package or base image. Each exception must be one exact CVE ID and include an
# owner, rationale, upstream tracking URL, and expiry date in the immediately
# preceding comments, using this exact shape:
# owner: @github-handle
# expires: YYYY-MM-DD
# tracking: https://upstream.example/issue
# rationale: No patched release exists; compensating control ...
# CVE-YYYY-NNNN
#
# Wildcards, GHSA aliases, and severity-wide suppressions are prohibited.

# owner: @ian-t-adams
# expires: 2026-10-31
# tracking: https://github.com/dotnet/dotnet-docker/issues/7384
# rationale: No patched release exists; Microsoft has not rebuilt the pinned .NET 10 noble-chiseled runtime (proxy and CompanionApp) with Ubuntu's fixed libssl3t64 3.0.13-0ubuntu3.16 (USN-8847), and the chiseled image has no package manager. Compensating control: the flaw is limited to OpenSSL DTLS handshake retransmission; the runtime's only libssl consumer is the .NET crypto shim, which binds TLS_method and no DTLS symbol, the image ships no msquic or openssl CLI, and neither app uses DTLS, QUIC, HTTP/3 or UDP. Refresh both runtime pins and delete this entry when the rebuilt image ships (AI4IA #552).
CVE-2026-84782
